            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "It looks like when tmux control mode is active in Wezterm (20260802-174340-fa0a1da0), it sends two different responses to the DA1 inside `terminfo_disable`:\n```bash\n$ printf '\\e[0c' && cat -v\n^[[?1;2;4c^[[?65;4;6;18;22;52c\n```\nWe only process events until we get the first one (ending in `4c`) and then continue stopping the tui. Not sure this is really a problem with nvim. On iTerm2, I see only `^[[?1;2c` as the response. Seems like it could be a tmux or WezTerm bug.",
            "created_at": "2026-08-08T02:16:32Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41220#issuecomment-5224037938",
